  "body": "## What changed\n\nThree user-reported issues after the 5.0.1 release:\n\n### 1. Windows install failed with `os error 32` mid-uv\n\n`uv tool install --force` overwrites every launcher shim in `~/.local/bin`; Windows cannot overwrite a running `.exe`. A live launcher (the proxy or an `fcc-claude`/`fcc-codex`/`fcc-pi` child) made uv fail partway with a cryptic error, leaving the tool env half-replaced. Both installers now detect running launchers **up front** (`Get-Process` in PS, `pgrep`/`ps` in sh), covering both command families, and abort **before** uv mutates anything, naming every running process. Reuses the uninstaller's `Assert-NoFccProcessesRunning` pattern.\n\n### 2. Post-install message led with legacy `fcc` commands\n\nNow leads with the native `mcc` family and short usage (`mcc-server`, `mcc-claude`, `mcc-codex`, `mcc-pi`, `mcc-claude --discover-models`), and no longer advertises `fcc` names.\n\n### 3. Dashboard showed \"Current vunknown\"\n\n`current_version()` read only the native distribution (`my-claude-code`), so a migration install still running the legacy `free-claude-code` tool reported nothing. It now tries native then legacy, so a mid-migration server always reports its real version. The uv receipt and extras lookup are owner-aware too, so extras and the Python pin are carried from whichever owner is installed.\n\n## Verification\n\nA live install with the user's real `fcc-claude`/`fcc-server` running is now blocked up front:\n```\n==> Checking for running My Claude Code processes\nMy Claude Code is still running (fcc-server, fcc-claude). Stop those processes, then rerun install.\n```\ninstead of `os error 32`. The guard passes when nothing is running (verified independently). `ruff`/`ty` clean. Full suite: 17 failed / 3660 passed — **identical failure set to unmodified main (17 failed / 3576 passed)**, so zero regressions; the +84 passing are the new tests.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The running-launcher guard matches process names globally (not per bin-dir), which is exactly the scope needed — a running proxy child is what blocks uv regardless of which dir it launched from.\n- On the user's machine, two real launchers are running (`fcc-claude` PID 21532, `fcc-server` PID 38588 from `C:\\tmp\\fcc-v5-test` — the latter a stray test server, not the live WSL `:8082`). They must be stopped for the install to proceed; that's now a clear message instead of a cryptic error.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
