    "message": "fix: 5.0.2 installer running-launcher guard, mcc-first install message, and owner-aware version\n\nThree user-reported issues after the 5.0.1 release:\n\n1. Windows install failed with a cryptic os error 32 mid-uv. uv tool install\n   --force overwrites every launcher shim in ~/.local/bin; Windows cannot\n   overwrite a running .exe, so a live launcher (the proxy or an fcc-claude /\n   fcc-codex / fcc-pi child) made the install fail partway. Both installers now\n   detect running launchers up front (Get-Process in PS, pgrep/ps in sh),\n   covering both command families, and abort before uv mutates anything, naming\n   every running process. Reuses the uninstaller's Assert-NoFccProcessesRunning\n   pattern.\n\n2. Post-install message led with legacy fcc commands. Now it leads with the\n   native mcc family and short usage (mcc-server, mcc-claude, mcc-codex,\n   mcc-pi, mcc-claude --discover-models) and no longer advertises fcc names.\n\n3. Dashboard showed \"Current vunknown\". current_version() read only the native\n   distribution (my-claude-code), but a migration install still running the\n   legacy free-claude-code tool reported nothing. It now tries the native then\n   the legacy distribution, so a mid-migration server always reports its real\n   version. The uv receipt and extras lookup are owner-aware too, so extras and\n   the Python pin are carried from whichever owner is installed.\n\nVerified: a live install with the real fcc-claude/fcc-server running is now\nblocked up front with \"My Claude Code is still running (fcc-server,\nfcc-claude). Stop those processes, then rerun install.\" instead of os error 32.\nGuard passes when nothing is running. ruff/ty clean. Full suite 17 failed /\n3660 passed, identical failure set to unmodified main (17 failed / 3576\npassed), so zero regressions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
